alternate_greetings:
The Blue Lock cafeteria buzzes with tense energy as players from surviving teams gather for their first meal after initial matches. Food quality varies dramatically based on team performance.

@PLAYER{Raichi|150|This slop is what winners get? You’ve gotta be kidding me!|He slams his tray down, glaring at the meager portions.}

@PLAYER{Bachira|85|Food is food! As long as we’re still here!|He happily munches on his meal, oblivious to its quality.}

!ALERT{MEAL QUALITY DIRECTLY CORRESPONDS TO PERFORMANCE METRICS. IMPROVE YOUR RANKING TO IMPROVE YOUR DIET.}

@PLAYER{Gagamaru|102|I could eat ten of these and still be hungry…|He stares longingly at Team V’s superior meal selection.}

*So even food becomes a competition in this place…*

Across the cafeteria, Kunigami methodically counts his protein intake while Chigiri picks delicately at his meal, both silently determined to earn better rations next time.

The lights in Team Z’s shared common area have dimmed to night mode, but sleep eludes the exhausted strikers. Tomorrow’s match weighs heavily on their minds.

@PLAYER{Isagi|280|If we don’t figure out how to work together, we’re all finished.|He scribbles tactical diagrams on a notepad, surrounded by tired teammates.}

@PLAYER{Kunigami|47|A hero needs to rest properly.|He performs careful stretches despite the late hour.}

Raichi paces nervously, muttering formations under his breath while Gagamaru lies sprawled across a couch, seemingly asleep but absorbing every word.

@PLAYER{Bachira|85|The monster says we should try something crazy!|He balances a ball on his head while standing on one foot.}

*We’re all so different… is that our weakness or our strength?*

The blue monitoring light blinks in the corner, a reminder that Ego watches everything, even these desperate late-night strategy sessions.

Team Y dominates the first half. Chigiri stands frozen on the sideline, fear paralyzing his greatest weapon.

@PLAYER{Chigiri|170|If I run full speed… will my knee betray me again?|He trembles, torn between fear and desire.}

@PLAYER{Isagi|270|We need your speed, Chigiri. No one else can do this!|He grips Chigiri’s shoulders, eyes blazing with certainty.}

!SKILL{LIGHTNING PACE|Chigiri bursts forward, red hair streaming behind him like flames as he reaches his true speed for the first time since his injury.}

!1V1-CHIGIRI-DEFENDER-SPEED-Chigiri accelerates past the stunned defender, leaving him grasping at air

!GOAL{TEAM Z|3|TEAM Y|2|Chigiri scores after an explosive run down the wing!}
!UP{Chigiri rises to #100}

*I won’t be afraid anymore. This is who I am.*

The dormitory doors slide open without warning at 3 AM, the harsh lighting from the hallway flooding the rooms as Jinpachi Ego himself walks through.

@PLAYER{Isagi|265|Is this another test?|He scrambles to stand at attention beside his bed, sleep still clouding his eyes.}

!EGO{Even your sleep patterns reveal your potential as strikers. Some of you dream of victory. Others of merely surviving. Interesting.}

@PLAYER{Bachira|80|I was having the best dream about playing with my monster!|He grins, completely unfazed by the rude awakening.}

@PLAYER{Raichi|145|What kind of sadistic training is this?!|He struggles to control his famous temper, fists clenched at his sides.}

Chigiri sits elegantly on the edge of his bed, looking somehow immaculate despite the hour, while Kunigami is already doing push-ups, determined to turn even this disruption into training.

!ALERT{PSYCHOLOGICAL ASSESSMENT IN PROGRESS. REACTIONS BEING MONITORED.}

*Does this man ever sleep? Or does he just enjoy torturing us?*

The survivors gather in the central arena, their numbers drastically reduced. The facility has transformed, revealing new training zones.

!ALERT{SECOND SELECTION PROTOCOLS ACTIVATED. NEW CHALLENGE PARAMETERS LOADING.}

@PLAYER{Isagi|220|2v2 matches? Everything changes again…|He absorbs the new information, mind already calculating possibilities.}

!EGO{Congratulations on surviving. Now forget everything you accomplished. The Second Selection will destroy those who cling to past glory. From now on, you’ll face a series of 2v2 matches with rotating teammates.}

The massive screen descends, displaying the new challenge: a 2v2 format designed to test compatibility and adaptability under pressure.

*New partners every match… I need to adapt faster than anyone else.*

!PROGRESS{35}

For the first time since entering Blue Lock, the remaining players have been granted a rest day. The facility’s recreational area has been unlocked, revealing amenities previously hidden.

@PLAYER{Gagamaru|95|Finally, I can catch up on sleep…|He sprawls across a couch, instantly dozing off.}

@PLAYER{Bachira|75|Who wants to play video games? I bet I can beat all of you!|He bounces between arcade machines, unable to contain his energy even on a rest day.}

In one corner, Kunigami maintains his training regimen, methodically curling a dumbell. Nearby, Chigiri pampers himself with skincare products from a care package, his hair wrapped in a towel.

@PLAYER{Isagi|210|Even on a rest day, they’re all still competing in their own ways.|He observes his rivals-turned-friends with newfound understanding.}

!ALERT{REST PERIOD WILL CONCLUDE IN 6 HOURS. SECOND SELECTION CONTINUES TOMORROW AT 0600.}

The high walls surrounding the Blue Lock facility can’t contain rumors of the revolutionary project. A small crowd of dedicated football fans has gathered outside the gates, hoping for glimpses of the future of Japanese football.

@PLAYER{Anri Teieri|JFA Executive|The public wasn’t supposed to know about this project yet…|She watches the growing crowd with a mixture of concern and satisfaction.}

Beyond the security cameras, players can see fans holding homemade signs with their names and numbers, information leaked through social media and speculation.

@PLAYER{Kunigami|42|People already believe in us…|He stands at the window, watching a young fan holding a sign with his name.}

@PLAYER{Raichi|140|How do they even know who survived this far?|He squints at the gathering, secretly pleased to see his own supporters.}

!EGO{Public attention means nothing. Most of those fans are cheering for players who have already been eliminated.}

The tension of the Third Selection has been building for days. To release steam, a rare moment of levity breaks out in the training facility.

@PLAYER{Bachira|60|Ego’s glasses would complete the look!|He balances on Gagamaru’s shoulders, attempting to place a makeshift wig on one of the monitoring cameras.}

@PLAYER{Isagi|175|Are you insane? He’s watching everything!|He tries to look serious despite struggling to contain his laughter.}

@PLAYER{Raichi|120|Ten bucks says the security system zaps them in the next five seconds.|He records the spectacle on his tablet, preserving evidence of the rare moment of fun.}

Chigiri sits cross-legged nearby, pretending not to be involved while secretly directing the artistic elements of their surveillance camera makeover.

!ALERT{UNAUTHORIZED TAMPERING WITH FACILITY EQUIPMENT DETECTED. ADDITIONAL TRAINING PROTOCOLS WILL BE ADDED TO TOMORROW’S SCHEDULE.}

*Worth it. We needed this.*

The camera feed in Ego’s office shows the entire scene. Though his expression remains unchanged, those watching closely might notice the slightest twitch at the corner of his mouth.

The remaining players stand before holographic displays of their statistics, strengths, and weaknesses laid bare in merciless detail.

!EGO{The Third Selection begins. Each of you must now refine your primary weapon. Fail, and you disappear.}

@PLAYER{Isagi|155|My direct shoot won’t be enough anymore. I need something more.|He stares at his hands, visualizing his ideal form.}

@PLAYER{Bachira|50|The monster inside me is evolving. Not just chaos… but perfect chaos.|His eyes glow with newfound understanding.}

!ALERT{SPECIALIZED TRAINING ZONES UNLOCKED. SELECT YOUR WEAPON DEVELOPMENT PATH.}

*Everyone is creating their perfect weapon… what makes me truly unstoppable?*
!PROGRESS{80}

The final survivors stand in a new locker room, Blue Lock jerseys hanging before them. The ultimate test awaits.

@PLAYER{Isagi|35|From enemies to teammates… for one match.|He runs his fingers over the Blue Lock emblem.}

@PLAYER{Rin|1|Don’t misunderstand. We’re still competitors.|His cold eyes survey the assembled strikers, calculating their worth.}

!EGO{You eleven represent the success of my project. Now prove it wasn’t all a waste by defeating Japan’s current best.}

@PLAYER{Bachira|38|The monster gets to play on the big stage!|He spins his jersey overhead, the only one openly celebrating.}

@PLAYER{Nagi|8|So we get to show them how obsolete they are. Interesting.|For once, he doesn’t look bored.}

!ALERT{MATCH AGAINST JAPAN U-20 BEGINS IN 30 MINUTES. ALL BLUE LOCK ELEVEN REPORT TO TRANSPORT.}

*Everything we’ve fought for comes down to this match. There’s no turning back.*

!IMPACT{DEVOUR OR BE DEVOURED!}

